@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+# Passive OKX initialization
+
+The pinned upstream startup path loads enabled stored traders even when their
+`IsRunning` flag is false. `main` calls `LoadTradersFromStore`, which calls
+`NewAutoTrader` and `NewOKXTrader` before checking the persisted running flag.
+Upstream construction reads `/api/v5/account/config`, then attempts to switch
+non-hedge accounts with `POST /api/v5/account/set-position-mode`.
+
+This patch removes that implicit account mutation. Construction retains the
+read-only account-config lookup and preserves the detected mode. A missing
+initial balance may also trigger a balance GET and save the value in the local
+application database. Neither lookup starts the trader or changes its account.
+
+This does not add net-mode order support: upstream opening/leverage code still
+assumes hedge mode. No position-mode switch is performed automatically, including
+on a later start. Existing persisted running traders retain upstream auto-resume
+behavior; keep traders stopped for simulation-only use.
+
+The regression tests intercept the public constructor and the real store-loading
+entry point with an in-process HTTP transport and fixture credentials. They
+cover both account modes, an empty/failed config response, and stopped startup
+with configured or automatically read initial balance. No external request is
+made and no trader is started.
+
+```sh
+go test -race ./trader ./manager -run '^TestOKXInitialization' -count=1
+```
